# Example ReRDMFT input file: water molecule, evaluating the GNOF
# (Piris natural orbital functional, Occ_opt/PNOFs.h) RDMFT functional
# on the converged approximate X2C-HF spinors -- same idea as
# water_gnof.inp/co-sto-3g_gnof.inp's own NON_REL/C4_DHF runs, just for
# X2C (see README.md's "X2C decoupling and X2C-HF" section): the
# converged X2C-HF orbitals/MO-basis integrals are held FIXED, the PNOF
# orbital subspaces are built with PNOF_COUPLING 2 (HOMO coupled with
# LUMO alone), and the geminal occupations are OPTIMIZED at those same
# fixed orbitals via Occ_opt/SQP.h -- printed right after the X2C-HF
# Hessian_opt cross-check section. Like NON_REL (and unlike C4_DHF),
# every X2C-HF spinor competes for occupation, since X2C's own
# decoupling already eliminated the negative-energy branch entirely.
NELEC 10
BASIS water-sto-3g.gbs
X2C TRUE
FUNCTIONAL GNOF
PNOF_COUPLING 2

GEOMETRY
O   0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
H   0.000000   0.757000   0.586000
H   0.000000  -0.757000   0.586000
END
